From 8f09a8ba39399e2c1f20df5531378691f6e98de7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:11:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] validation(v2): memoize exact BIP340 verification through the
 host signature cache

The original native VM bypassed the existing bounded signature cache; this is a new focused native optimization, not recovered lost wiring. Both policy and consensus VM executions, derived signing messages, branch proofs, encoding rules, cost/deferred records and context checks still run. Only a successful exact cryptographic operation is reusable, keyed by independent native domain, full message/key/signature and mint encoding context. Existing cache salt, size limits and store/erase semantics apply; failures never insert.

The VM stays host-neutral: an optional non-owning synchronous verifier is never retained in prepared contexts. Null verifier uses the original pure function; simulation and batch-collector paths retain precedence. No general VM-verdict reuse, consensus flag reuse, new globals, thread pools or RPC option.

Current matched ABC/native samples show direct native verification in both policy and consensus. The regression uses real matured native funding, existing signature-cache metrics, both flag sets without whole-script caching, and changed coins/signature/encoding/key/message/mint/domain/non-storing controls.

Test-only integration correction: explicitly qualify global ::Coin to avoid the native model name collision; all assertions and production bytes unchanged.

Coordinator causal regression coverage for earlier prepared-VM owner112: retain one resolved-coins wrapper, reconstruct a changed signed transaction at the exact same address without resigning, assert full hash changes and authoritative CheckInput rejects. Production fullTxHash cache-binding repair belongs112; this existing native crypto fixture supplies the late prerequisite. No additional crypto behavior or whole-VM verdict reuse.
